### Use with the "REST Client" extension in VS Code.
### The server must be running: npm run dev
### Reset data anytime with: npm run seed

@base = http://localhost:3000/api

### ---------- S6.1 — List books (10 pts) ----------
GET {{base}}/books

### All books (expect 5 books)
GET {{base}}/books

### Search filter (expect 1 book: "Learning JavaScript")
GET {{base}}/books?search=java

### ---------- S6.2 — Member with loans (10 pts) ----------

### Member 1 with loans (expect Sok Dara with 2 loans)
GET {{base}}/members/6

### Unknown member (expect 404)
GET {{base}}/members/999

### ---------- S6.3 — Borrow report, raw SQL (15 pts) ----------

### Expect on fresh seed:
### Learning JavaScript = 2, Khmer Empire History = 1,
### Database Design Basics = 1, Node.js in Action = 1,
### Web Development for Beginners = 0
GET {{base}}/reports/borrowed-books

### ---------- S7.1 — Borrow a book (25 pts) ----------

### Happy path (expect 201, dueDate = today + 14 days,
### then GET /books shows book 4 copiesAvailable 2 -> 1)
POST {{base}}/loans
Content-Type: application/json

{ "memberId": 3, "bookId": 4 }

### No copies available: book 5 has 0 (expect 409)
POST {{base}}/loans
Content-Type: application/json

{ "memberId": 1, "bookId": 5 }

### Unknown member (expect 404)
POST {{base}}/loans
Content-Type: application/json

{ "memberId": 999, "bookId": 1 }

### Unknown book (expect 404)
POST {{base}}/loans
Content-Type: application/json

{ "memberId": 1, "bookId": 999 }

### ---------- S7.2 — Return a loan (10 pts) ----------

### Happy path: loan 1 is BORROWED (expect 200, status RETURNED,
### returnDate set, then GET /books shows book 1 copies 2 -> 3)
PUT {{base}}/loans/1/return

### Return the same loan again (expect 409)
PUT {{base}}/loans/1/return

### Unknown loan (expect 404)
PUT {{base}}/loans/999/return
